It is Wednesday evening and I am walking home from the bus stop.
I stop at my usual market to buy fresh vegetables.
The market is bustling as always.
I go to my favourite vegetable vendor's cart.
"Namaste Madam, what do you want today?" he asks.
"Namaste Dada, give me half a kilo of tomatoes," I say.
"And are these potatoes fresh?" I ask, pointing to the basket.
"Yes Madam, they arrived just this morning," he says.
"Then give me one kilo of potatoes and some green chillies too," I tell him.
He packs the vegetables in my cloth bag.
I also take a bunch of fresh coriander.
"Dada, how much is the total?" I ask him.
"One hundred and twenty rupees," he replies.
I give him the money and smile.
Without my asking, Dada adds the coriander I like to the bag.
I set off before the evening rain begins.
I take my bag and happily walk towards my building.
